boundaries.note:
Established BY CONSTRUCTION rather than inferred: `NotificationCollector.push/3` then `drain/1` returns `[%{"jsonrpc" => "2.0", "method" => "notifications/message", "params" => %{"level" => "info"}}]`, and plug.ex:426 drains the collector into `send_response/4` -> `send_sse_response/3` at :1008, whose :1010 is `(notifications ++ [response]) |> Enum.map_join(&SSE.encode_message/1)`. Run at this tip, that emits the bytes `event: message
data: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"notifications/message","params":{"level":"info"}}

` into the HTTP response body. The mutation reddened only its own unit because the one live test that could have caught it, streamable_http_stateless_test.exs:299, is a REFUTE of a notification's presence — renaming the key leaves the refute passing. Same directional failure as S7-16.

